"{\n  \"AND\": {\n    \"left\": {\n      \"OR\": {\n        \"left\": {\n          \"raw_text\": \"Patients with any other primary DSM-IV psychiatric diagnosis in addition to Obsessive Compulsive Disorder.\"\n        },\n        \"right\": {\n          \"AND\": {\n            \"left\": {\n              \"OR\": {\n                \"left\": {\n                  \"raw_text\": \"Patients who currently fulfil criteria for DSM-IV eating disorder, body dysmorphic disorder, current alcohol or substance abuse, or who have a lifetime history of bipolar disorder. Patients with a history of Schizophrenia and other psychotic disorders, Delirium, Dementia, and Amnestic and other cognitive disorders.\"\n                },\n                \"right\": {\n                  \"OR\": {\n                    \"left\": {\n                      \"raw_text\": \"Subjects with a concurrent Axis II Cluster A Personality Disorder\"\n                    },\n                    \"right\": {\n                      \"OR\": {\n                        \"left\": {\n                          \"raw_text\": \"Borderline or Antisocial Personality Disorder.\"\n                        }\n                      }\n                    }\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"right\": {\n          \"AND\": {\n            \"left\": {\n              \"OR\": {\n                \"left\": {\n                  \"raw text\": \"Subjects who based on history or mental status examination have a significant risk of committing suicide, in the investigator's opinion.\"\n                },\n                \"right\": {\n                  \"OR\": {\n                    \"left\": {\n                      \"raw text\": \"Subjects with a history of more than three adequate trials with an SSRI.\"\n                    },\n                    \"right\": {\n                      \"OR\": {\n                        \"raw text\": \"Subjects who have had an adequate trial of pregabalin.\"\n                    }\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"right\": {\n          \"AND\": {\n            \"left\": {\n              \"OR\": {\n                \"left\": {\n                  \"raw text\": \"Subjects who have initiated psychotherapy in the last 4 months prior to the first visit.\"\n                },\n                \"right\": {\n                  \"OR\": {\n                    \"raw text\": \"Subjects who, during the course of the study, would be likely to require treatment with prohibited concomitant therapy.\"\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"right\": {\n          \"AND\": {\n            \"left\": {\n              \"OR\": {\n                \"left\": {\n                  \"raw text\": \"Prior use of or a known allergy or hypersensitivity to pregabalin.\"\n                },\n                \"right\": {\n                  \"OR\": {\n                    \"raw text\": \"Subjects who have participated in any clinical trial within 30 days prior to entering the study, or in a clinical trial involving a psychotropic medication within the 6 months prior to entering the study.\"\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"right\": {\n          \"AND\": {\n            \"left\": {\n              \"OR\": {\n                \"left\": {\n                  \"raw text\": \"Any subject who has been taking benzodiazepines before entering the study who: 1) cannot tolerate being free of benzodiazepines for 4 weeks, or 2) has signs or symptoms of benzodiazepine withdrawal or rebound at the end of those 4 weeks. Should a patient entering the study, who is currently on benzodiazepines develop discontinuation symptoms with discontinuation of their benzodiazepine, we will treat these symptoms with a more gradual benzodiazepine taper. Study will be delayed until the patient is able to tolerate the discontinuation for 4 weeks.\"\n                },\n                \"right\": {\n                  \"OR\": {\n                    \"raw text\": \"Patients with a current seizure disorder, organic brain disorder or a history of seizure disorders (except for febrile seizures in childhood). Patients with thyroid pathology, the treatment of which has not been stabilized for at least three months. Patients on neuroleptic drugs in the two months prior to study entry or cognitive behavioural therapy specific to OCD within four weeks of study entry Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to pregabalin. Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients with a history of major depression and suicidal ideation or behaviour, or with current suicidal ideation or behaviour or a history of suicidal behaviour or attempt by themselves or first degree relatives. Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients with known angle closure glaucoma. Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients taking strong CYP3A4 inducers (e.g. Rifampicin, St John's Wort). Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients taking strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (e.g. Cimetidine, fluoxetine). Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients taking carbapenem antibiotics (e.g. Imipenem, meropenem, etrapenem, doripenem). Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients taking proton pump inhibitors (e.g. Omeprazole, lansoprazole, pantoprazole, rabeprazole, esomeprazole). Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients taking hormonal contraceptives (e.g. The pill, patch, or ring). Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients with a history of major surgery for the treatment of malignancy, unless they have fully recovered from the treatment. Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients with a history of angle closure glaucoma. Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients taking strong CYP3A4 inducers (e.g. Rifampicin, St John's Wort). Pregabalin is contraindicated in patients taking strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (e.g. Cimetidine, fl